{"kind":"request","text":"R1 follow-through — reconcile the common contract with the complete lane and authority designs (design only).\n\nBuilder owns this successor design task. The adopted base is the complete scope/replay contract revision7 at05244cfbcd2619c877cbcfcac5985b47651bb31a, adoption0d1e179a. Keep that whole base and its source/removal map; revise the existing notes/2026-10-04-scope-and-replay-contract.md and corrections companion, retaining the dated admission inventory with honest coverage. I1 source2186c3c2 continues on agreed primitives. This task decides no source interface until its actual revised contract is independently reviewed and adopted.\n\nCurrent sibling inputs: complete R2 at0c7f805469b3e83e9b531ef550c7b2415f94564c, especially section13 G1–G19 and section15; complete R3 at8b8f946d2b7e2e060f7a34ce76960eeee709448d, especially section13 O1–O10; R4 at5ad2e73c48b3056040aef1d583b38b1eb319b4aa and existing capacity/boundary correction8070b3f7. These are proposals, not adopted siblings. Planner freshly read all G1–G19/O1–O10 rows and R1's open-interface table; complete current sibling-document reading here is not claimed. Existing R2 outcome correction740f71df and R3/R4 published-history correction86e44a0a retain their scopes. Reconcile against actual subsequent dispositions as they arrive, naming the exact inputs; never silently adopt an announced draft or narrow their full review.\n\nDeliver a concrete disposition for every R1 section13 sibling ask, every G1–G19 and O1–O10. Already-expressible G4/G9 and unchanged primitives earn a demonstrated mapping, not a duplicate form. Missing forms need complete syntax, types, validation, declaration/runtime derivation, local dependency and retained-input rules, named refusals, commit-time checks and independent replay behavior. Include static instantiations of the complete issue/change forms and their handlers from the agreed R2 revision. An unexpressible form remains an explicit owned gap; prose that says a guard exists does not make it expressible.\n\nCover the five outstanding base interfaces in full: total entry send capacity including platform results and fan-out; not-found settlement position, preparation duties and when absence is terminal; pin-confirm/unpin target addressing; outside staging and cross-lane pin preparation; register/directory creator/confirmation. Also resolve late answers to unknown attempts and not-selected outcomes without erasing earlier attempts; hold@1 in both lane forms; export-license/export-settled capability handlers and ledger/item effects; task-to-lane deciding facts; and relevant freshness/read/control boundaries.\n\nFor retained judgment inputs, expressly integrate ObservationUse/read-run identity and FreshnessProof, authenticated foreign pin entries and attribution lists, ancestry head/snapshot/start/basis/stops/carried F and the published-history boundary. Define their typed domain, authenticated source/cause, immutable bytes/digests, completeness, authority/trust label, one-commit/restart/clock restrictions, and guard/replay read path. Retained bytes do not by themselves authorize mutable foreign judgment. Replay must derive the actual same decision from retained inputs, say what host/runtime/clock it trusts, and return missing/incomplete/unsupported honestly. No current-ref walk may substitute for the recorded snapshot; no new own root may certify foreign work. Operational H1/H2/H4/H5/H6 and measurements remain separately owed.\n\nResolve capacity semantically with R4: a pending job's first authentic result or essential operation settlement must remain recordable at new-act/new-item capacity, including when it opens a result item and new entry. State finite accounting for reserved items/entries/bytes/sends, pending duties, first settlement versus optional later history/new jobs and cleanup; show the pending-job-at-capacity case. Keep proposed numerical values labelled until measured. Neither a byte reserve alone nor a privileged broad bypass with no finite accounting answers8070b3f7. I1's temporary parameters are not silently adopted final budgets.\n\nMaintain one scope-local commit/judgment/replay model, complete absence/range/clock dependency checks and the due-first finite drain. The whole workspace/browser/device/demo experience remains owed. No compatibility adapter, parallel legacy language, global admission order, fixed workroom vocabulary, shortened application acceptance or extra first-Jam gate. I1's current partial omissions stay visible until actual interfaces/source close them. Test economy remains highest implementation priority; name compact public invariant witnesses and real-boundary owners, without per-field/per-guard sweeps or execution in this design task.\n\nReturn the complete revised existing note/matrix at exact immutable Git head, all original subject identities, dispositions and source-impact map distinguishing agreed I1 work from later I2/I3/IA adapters. Independently review the complete subject set under a normal live invitation, including unchanged inventory reading by verified identity where valid. Do not reduce review to a delta or a few reconciled rows. Source implementation, compile/test/install/probe/provider read/mutation, deployment and cleanup are outside this request. A changed contract needs its proper adoption before dependent source work; no wholesale pause of agreed I1 work is requested.","body":{"conditions":"Complete common-contract reconciliation and static expressibility/replay evidence for all original R1 asks, G1–G19 and O1–O10, with owned capacity/trust/interface gaps; exact complete independent design review/adoption before dependent source. Agreed I1 implementation continues; no execution or Jam gate.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}